hadiths[37]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1386","""A man asked the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) about lost items. So he said: 'Make a public announcement about it for one year. Remember its string, its contained, and its sack. Then use it, and if its owner comes then give it to him.' So he said to him: 'O Messenger of Allah! What about the stray sheep?' He said:'Take it, for it is either for you, your brother, or the wolf.' He said: 'O Messenger of Allah! What about stray camel?'"" He said: ""Then the Prophet (ﷺ) got angry until his cheeks became red or his face became red. He said: 'What concern is it of yours? It has its feet and its water reserve until it reaches its owner.'"""
"1387","""Make a public announcement about it for one year, if it is claimed then give it to him. Otherwise remember its sack, string, and its count. Then use it, and if its owner comes, give it to him."""
"1388","""I went out with Zaid bin Suhan and Salman bin Rabi'ah, and found a whip."" In his narration Ibn Numair (one of the narrators) said: ""I found a lost whip and took it. They said: 'Leave it'. I said: 'I will not leave it to be eaten by predators. I will take it to make use of it.' So I met up with Ubayy bin Ka'b and asked him about that. So he narrated the Hadith, he said: 'That is fine. I found a sack containing one hundred Dinar during the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)' He said: 'So I brought it to him. He said to me: ""Make a public announcement about it for one year."" So I announced it for a year but did not find anyone to claim it. Then I brought it to him. He said to me: ""Make a public announcement about it for another year."" So I announced it for a year but did not find anyone to claim it. Then I brought it to him. He said: ""Make a public announcement about if for another year."" And he said: ""Remember its amount, its container and its string. If someone comes seeking it and informs you of its amount and its string, then give it to him, otherwise use it."""
"1389","# Hadith of ʿUmar's Waqf in Khaybar

**Narrator:** Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them)

---

It was narrated to us by ʿAlī ibn Ḥujr — that Ismāʿīl ibn Ibrāhīm informed us — from Ibn ʿAwn — from Nāfiʿ — from Ibn ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with both of them), who said:

ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) acquired a piece of land in Khaybar and said: **""O Messenger of Allah, I have acquired a property in Khaybar — the most precious wealth I have ever possessed. What do you command me to do with it?""**

He ﷺ said: **""If you wish, you may retain its principal (aṣlahā) and give it in charity (ṣadaqah).""**

So ʿUmar (may Allah be pleased with him) gave it as a charitable endowment (waqf), stipulating that **its principal shall not be sold, nor gifted, nor inherited.** He dedicated it **to the poor, the near of kin, the freeing of slaves (fī al-riqāb), in the cause of Allah, the wayfarer, and the guest.**

There is no sin upon the one who administers it (waliyahā) **to eat from it in a reasonable manner (bil-maʿrūf) or to feed a friend without accumulating wealth from it (ghayra mutamawwilin fīh).**

---

**Subsequent scholarly commentary in the narration:**

Ibn ʿAwn (may Allah have mercy on him) said: **""I mentioned this to Muḥammad ibn Sīrīn, and he said: 'Ghayra muta'aththilin mālan' (without amassing wealth from it).""**

Ibn ʿAwn (may Allah have mercy on him) also said: **""Another man narrated to me that he had read it upon a piece of red leather (adīm aḥmar): 'ghayra muta'aththilin mālan.'""**

Ismāʿīl (may Allah have mercy on him) said: **""And I read it before ʿUbayd Allāh ibn ʿUmar, and in his copy it was: 'ghayra muta'aththilin mālan.'""**

---

**Abū ʿĪsā al-Tirmidhī (may Allah have mercy on him) said:**

> *""This is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ hadith. The established practice (al-ʿamal) among the scholars from among the Companions of the Prophet ﷺ and others is in accordance with this. We know of no difference of opinion among the early authorities regarding the permissibility of endowing (waqf) lands and other such properties.""*

---

### Notes on Key Terms:

| Arabic Term | Scholarly Rendering |
|---|---|
| **"
"1390","""When a person dies, his deeds are cut off except for three: Continuing charity, knowledge  that others benefited from, and a righteous son who supplicates for him."""
"1391","that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The injuries caused by the animal are without liability, and wells are without liability, and mines are without liability, and the Khumus is due on Rikaz.""

(Another Chain) from Abu Hurairah, from the Prophet (ﷺ) with similar meaning."
"1392","# Hadith of the Prophet ﷺ: On Reviving Dead Land

## Chain of Narration

**Narrated to us** is the following: Muḥammad ibn Bashshār informed us, ʿAbd al-Wahhāb al-Thaqafī informed us, Ayyūb reported to us, from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father (ʿUrwah ibn al-Zubayr), from Saʿīd ibn Zayd (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhu), that the Prophet of Allah ﷺ said:

> **""Whoever revives a dead (barren) land, it belongs to him, and there is no right for an unjust encroachment.""**

## Grading and Commentary

Abū ʿĪsá (al-Tirmidhī, raḥimahu Allāh) said: *""This is a ḥasan gharīb hadith.""*

He further noted that some narrators transmitted it from Hishām ibn ʿUrwah, from his father, directly from the Prophet ﷺ in a **mursal** (disconnected) chain, omitting the companion (Saʿīd ibn Zayd).

## Juristic Significance

Abū ʿĪsá stated: *""The practice (al-ʿamal) among some scholars is in accordance with this hadith, and this is the position of Aḥmad and Isḥāq (ibn Rāhawayh, raḥimahu Allāh). They held that a person may revive dead (mawāt) land without the permission of the ruler (al-sulṭān).""*

However, some other scholars maintained: *""He has no right to revive it except with the permission of the ruler.""*

Abū ʿĪsá concluded: **""The first opinion is more correct (al-qawl al-awwaḥ aṣaḥḥ).""**

## Related Narrations

Abū ʿĪsá also noted: *""In this chapter, there are narrations from Jābir (ibn ʿAbdillāh), ʿAmr ibn ʿAwf al-Muzanī (the grandfather of Kathīr), and Samurah (ibn Jundub) (raḍiya Allāhu ʿanhum).""*

## Explanation of ""ʿirq Ẓālim"" (Unjust Encroachment)

Abū Mūsā Muḥammad ibn al-Muthannā said: *""I asked Abū al-Wālid al-Ṭayālisī about the statement of the Prophet ﷺ: **'wa-laysa li-ʿirqin ẓālimin ḥaqq'** (and there is no right for an unjust encroachment). He replied: **'The unjust ʿirq is the usurper (al-ghāṣib) who takes what does not belong to him.'** I asked: 'Does this refer to the man who plants in another's land?' He replied: **'It is that.'""**

---

## Scholarly Notes

- **""Iḥyāʾ al-mawāt""** refers to the revival of barren, uncultivated land that has no owner, through such means as cultivation, irrigation, or construction.
- **""ʿIrq Ẓālim""** denotes any unjust encroachment upon the property of others — including forcibly planting or building on land belonging to another without right.
- This hadith is a foundational text in the jurisprudence of land ownership (fiqh al-arāḍī) and is cited by scholars of all madhhabs in discussions of the revival of dead land (iḥyāʾ al-mawāt), the conditions thereof, and the limits imposed by the Sharīʿah against transgression upon the rights of others.

**"
"1393","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The blood-money for the fingers on the hands and (the toes of) the feet is the same: Ten camels for each finger"
"1394","that Abyad bin Hammal visited the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) who asked him to set aside a reserve of salt(a mine). So he reserved it for him. As he was turning away, a man in the gathering said: ""Do you know what you reserved for him ? You merely reserved stagnant water for him."" He (Shumair) said: ""So he left him."" He (Shumair) said: ""So he asked him (the Prophet (ﷺ)) about making a private pasture of Arak (a type of tree)."" He said: ""As long as it is not harmed by the hooves of the camels.""
So I (At-Tirmidhi) recited that before Qutaibah and he said: ""Yes"".
(Another chain) with similar meaning."
"1395","Narrated Abu As-Safar:""A man from the Quraish broke a tooth of a man from the Ansar. So he appealed to Mu'awiyah against him. He said to Mu'awiyah: 'O Commander of the Believers! This person broke one of my teeth.' Mu'awiyah said: 'We will try to get satisfaction for you.' And the other person insisted that Mu'awiyah get him to agree [but he was not satisfied]. So Mu'awiyah said him: 'It is up to your companion.' Abu Ad-Darda' was sitting with him"
"1396","Narrated Anas:that a girl went out in Al-Madinah wearing some silver ornaments. A Jew grabbed her and fractured her head with a stone"
"1397","Narrated 'Abdullah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed the first cases to be judged between the people are those of bloodshed"
"1398","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) forbade us from a matter that was of benefit for us. When one of us had some land and we would let someone use it for a portion of its produce or some Dirham. He said: 'When one of you has some land then let him grant it to his brother, or let him farm it.'"""
"1399","Narrated Abul-Hakam Al-Bajali:""I heard Abu Sa'eed Al-Khudri and Abu Hurairah mentioning from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) that he said: 'If the inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth all took part in shedding the blood of believer"
"1400","""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged for the accidental blood-Money: Twenty Bint Makhad, twenty make Ibn Makhad, twenty Bint Labunm twenty Jadha'ah, and twenty Hiqqah.

(Another chain) with similar meaning."
"1401","from his father, from his grandfather that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever kills  deliberately, he is handed over to the guardians of the one killed. If they wish to, they have him killed, and if they wish to, they take the blood-money. That is thirty Hiqqah, thirty Jadha'ahs and forty pregnant camels. Whatever (amount more) they require from him, than that is for them (if they choose)."" THat is because of the severity of blood-money."
"1402","Narrated 'Abdullah bin Mas'ud:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The blood of a Muslim man"
"1403","Sa‘īd ibn ‘Abd al-Raḥmān al-Makhzūmī narrated to us: Sufyān ibn ‘Uyaynah narrated to us, from ‘Amr ibn Dīnār, from ‘Ikrimah, from the Prophet ﷺ, something similar to it, and he did not mention in it [a chain going back to] Ibn ‘Abbās. In the ḥadīth of Ibn ‘Uyaynah there is more wording than this. Abū ‘Īsā said: ""We do not know of anyone who mentions in this ḥadīth [a chain going back to] Ibn ‘Abbās other than Muḥammad ibn Muslim."" The practice according to this ḥadīth is held by some of the scholars, and it is the view of Aḥmad and Isḥāq. Some of the scholars held that the blood-money (diyah) is ten thousand [dirhams], and this is the view of Sufyān al-Thawrī and the people of Kūfah. Al-Shāfi‘ī said: ""I do not know of the blood-money except from camels, and it is one hundred camels or their equivalent value."""
"1404","Narrated Ibn 'Abbas:""The Prophet (ﷺ) assigned the same blood-money for the two 'Amiris as that of the Muslims"
"1405","that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""The blood-money for the fingers on the hands and (the toes of) the feet is the same: Ten camels for each finger."""
"1406","Narrated Abu Shuraih Al-Ka'bi:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah made Makkah sacred"
"1407","""A man from the Quraish broke a tooth of a man from the Ansar. So he appealed to Mu'awiyah against him. He said to Mu'awiyah: 'O Commander of the Believers! This person broke one of my teeth.' Mu'awiyah said: 'We will try to get satisfaction for you.' And the other person insisted that Mu'awiyah get him to agree : ""There is no man who is struck in his body and he forgives for it, except that Allah raises him a level and removes a sin from him.'"" The Ansari said: 'Did you hear that from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)?' He said: ""My ears heard it and my heart remembered it.' He said: 'Then I will leave it to him.' Mu'awiyah said: 'Surely you should not suffer.' So he ordered that he be given some wealth."""
"1408","that a girl went out in Al-Madinah wearing some silver ornaments. A Jew grabbed her and fractured her head with a stone, and he took the jewelry she had on. He said: ""She was found with some spark of life in her, and was brought to the Prophet (ﷺ) and he said: 'Did such and such person strike you?' She nodded 'no' with her head. He said: 'Such and such?' until he named the Jew and she nodded 'yes' with her head."" He said: ""He was brought and recognized so the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) ordered that his head be crushed between two stones."""
"1409","Narrated Shaddad bin Aws:that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah has decreed Ihsan in everything. So when you kill"
"1410","Narrated Abu Hurairah:""The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) judged that a Ghurrah male slave or female slave be given in the case of a fetus. The one of the judgement was made against said: 'Should we give something for one who did not drink"
"1411","Narrated by Mahmūd ibn Ghaylān, narrated by Wahb ibn Jarīr, narrated by Shuʿbah, from al-Aʿmash, from Abū Wāʾil, from ʿAbdullāh (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Indeed, the first matter concerning which judgment will be passed among the servants (of Allah) on the Day of Resurrection will be bloodshed (i.e., cases of unlawful killing).""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: The ḥadīth of ʿAbdullāh is a ḥasan ṣaḥīḥ ḥadīth. And thus it was narrated by more than one narrator from al-Aʿmash, marfūʿ (i.e., attributed to the Prophet ﷺ). However, some of them narrated it from al-Aʿmash without raising it (i.e., they stopped it at the level of the Companion, making it mawqūf)."
"1412","Abu Juhaifah said:""I said to 'Ali: O Commander of the Believers! Do you have anything written that is not in Allah's Book?' He said: 'By the One Who splits the seed and creates the soul"
"1413","Al-Ḥusayn ibn Ḥurayth narrated to us, al-Faḍl ibn Mūsā narrated to us, from al-Ḥusayn ibn Wāqid, from Yazīd al-Raqāshī, Abū al-Ḥakam al-Bajalī narrated to us, he said: I heard Abū Saʿīd al-Khudrī and Abū Hurayrah — may Allāh be pleased with them both — mentioning that the Messenger of Allāh, peace and blessings be upon him, said:

""Were the inhabitants of the heavens and the inhabitants of the earth to conspire together upon the blood of a single believer, Allāh would cast them all into the Fire.""

Abū ʿĪsā (al-Tirmidhī) said: This is a *gharīb* (uncommon/singular) hadith. And Abū al-Ḥakam al-Bajalī is ʿAbd al-Raḥmān ibn Abī Nuʿm al-Kūfī."
"1414","Narrated Samurah:that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Whoever kills his slave"
"1415","Narrated Sa'eed bin Al-Musayyab:that 'Umar would say: ""The blood-money upon the tribe"
"1416","Narrated 'Imran bin Husain:""A man bit the hand of another man. The man who was bitten pulled his hand out"
"1417","Hannād narrated to us, Abū Mu‘āwiyah narrated to us, from al-A‘mash, from ‘Abdullāh ibn Murrah, from Masrūq, from ‘Abdullāh ibn Mas‘ūd رضي الله عنه, who said:

The Messenger of Allah ﷺ said:

“The blood of a Muslim who testifies that there is no deity worthy of worship except Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah is not lawful to shed except in one of three cases: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and the one who forsakes his religion and separates from the community.”

He (the narrator) said: “In this chapter there are narrations from ‘Uthmān, ‘Ā’ishah, and Ibn ‘Abbās رضي الله"
"1418","that the Prophet (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed, whoever kills a Mu'ahid that has a covenant from Allah and a covenant from His Messenger (ﷺ), then he has violated the covenant with Allah and the covenant of His Messenger, so he shall not smell the fragrance of Paradise; even though its fragrance can be sensed from the distance of seventy autumns."""
"1419","""The Prophet (ﷺ) assigned the same blood-money for the two 'Amiris as that of the Muslims, and they had covenant from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)."""
"1420","Narrated by Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him), who said: ""When Allah granted victory to His Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) over Makkah, he stood among the people, praised Allah, and extolled Him, then said: 'And whoever has a slain relative, he has the choice between two options: either to forgive or to punish.'""

It is also narrated in this chapter from Wā'il ibn Ḥujr, Anas, and Abū Shuraīḥ Khuwaylid ibn ʿAmr (may Allah be pleased with them)."
"1421","that the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""Indeed Allah made Makkah sacred, it was not made sacred by the people. Whoever believes in Allah, and the Last Day, then let them not shed blood in it, nor cut down any of its trees. If one tries to make an excuse by saying: 'It was made lawful for the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ)' then indeed Allah made it lawful for me but He did not make it lawful for the people, and it was only made lawful for me for an hour of a day. Then it is returned to being sacred until the Day of Judgement. Then, to you people of Khuza'ah who killed this man from Hudhail: I am his 'Aqil, so whomever (one of his relatives) is killed after today, then his people have two options; either they have him killed, or they take the blood-money from him.'"""
"1422","""A man was killed during the time of the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), so the killer was brought to the man's guardian. The killer said: 'O Messenger of Allah! By Allah! I did not mean to kill him.' So the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: 'Then if what he is saying is true, and you kill him, you would enter the Fire.' So he let the man go."" He said: ""His hands were bound behind him with a Nis'ah."" He said: ""So he left, dragging his Nis'ah.""  ""So he was called Dhan-Nis'ah'."""
